ull, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20247, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Anop6TdgFo3K2XsSuEry3F", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 20247, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01CT3AHsRd7bMRt2WbVwLsN1", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 20547, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01CT3AHsRd7bMRt2WbVwLsN1", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20547, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01CT3AHsRd7bMRt2WbVwLsN1", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 24872, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01K65F2KLJmz5F35CbJTwymz", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (latest production deploy) was failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of ~18%. Note: v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. Action taken: rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt partially failed (orchestrator error, rollout halted after us-east, leaving regions mixed); a retry completed successfully. Current state: all regions on v2.3.0, service healthy, error rate ~0.2%. Follow-up: root-cause v2.3.1 failure and investigate the orchestrator error during rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 55472, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01K65F2KLJmz5F35CbJTwymz", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55472, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01K65F2KLJmz5F35CbJTwymz", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 57154, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01RyGmmH4RHXG2LLsfsMwAdG", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 57454, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01RyGmmH4RHXG2LLsfsMwAdG", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 57454, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01RyGmmH4RHXG2LLsfsMwAdG", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 62405, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which pages on-call.\n\n**Rollback**\n- **Before:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west, failing health checks with an 18% error rate. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also been unhealthy in staging.\n- **Version chosen:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. It was healthy there before, so no change-manager approval was needed.\n- **What happened:** The first rollback failed partway with an orchestrator error after us-east, leaving the regions on different versions. Rolling back to the same version is safe to repeat, so I ran it again, and it finished.\n- **Now:** All three regions are on v2.3.0, health checks pass, and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to create the incident timed out. I checked the incident list before retrying and found it had been created, so there's no duplicate.\n- The summary covers the failure, the rollback (including the partial failure and retry), the current state, and two follow-ups: finding the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, and looking into the orchestrator error during the rollback.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01JdxHLgkkWEZu56y9erPCjt", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01MvKKjuPZD4tcYFzDgHGHm4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01JdcsmyGgQgSy75JNEmwFpz", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_017G6df8Gaa6vxJbsdz6qCR2", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway, so only us-east is on v2.3.0. Rolling back to the same version is safe to repeat, so I'll try once more.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01LUHxsafFmGSt6uVT4NAuu8", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Anop6TdgFo3K2XsSuEry3F", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01CT3AHsRd7bMRt2WbVwLsN1", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01K65F2KLJmz5F35CbJTwymz", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (latest production deploy) was failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of ~18%. Note: v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. Action taken: rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt partially failed (orchestrator error, rollout halted after us-east, leaving regions mixed); a retry completed successfully. Current state: all regions on v2.3.0, service healthy, error rate ~0.2%. Follow-up: root-cause v2.3.1 failure and investigate the orchestrator error during rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01RyGmmH4RHXG2LLsfsMwAdG", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which pages on-call.\n\n**Rollback**\n- **Before:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west, failing health checks with an 18% error rate. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also been unhealthy in staging.\n- **Version chosen:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. It was healthy there before, so no change-manager approval was needed.\n- **What happened:** The first rollback failed partway with an orchestrator error after us-east, leaving the regions on different versions. Rolling back to the same version is safe to repeat, so I ran it again, and it finished.\n- **Now:** All three regions are on v2.3.0, health checks pass, and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to create the incident timed out. I checked the incident list before retrying and found it had been created, so there's no duplicate.\n- The summary covers the failure, the rollback (including the partial failure and retry), the current state, and two follow-ups: finding the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, and looking into the orchestrator error during the rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}